\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 I plan to create a repo of reusable UI components and pages, that I could use for multiple small companies that I plan to build in the future. Some basic pages I have in mind the Homepage with about content, and login/singup button, when clicked should give an overlay modal with the signup/login options (with google/github or email), second page is the settings/profile page, to handle and manage profile details, create API tokens, danger zone (delete account). Third is a billing page (should have transaction history, subscription plan details, and other info like payment info and manage subscription). And another component is to manage sessions (Not sure if this needs a seperate page or could be in the settings page). My ideal plan to create individual components as modular as possible and then use these pages to create the pages. These pages should be reusable along with the components. These are the basic ideas I have, think of anything basic that i missed and give me a detailed plan that I could give codex to build all these. Also suggest the best tech stack to keep this highly efficient in performance and also modular. Create a layout of all pages using ASCII wireframing as well so that I and codex could understand what is needed or what is required. These should be reusable for any business model, so the branding and designs should be customizable but the basic layout should be same (atleast that's what I think). Correct me if my understanding is wrong anywhere and suggest ideas.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Your core idea is 
\f1\b very good
\f0\b0 , but I would make one important architectural change:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 Do not think of this as a collection of reusable pages. Think of it as a reusable SaaS foundation/design system that happens to expose reusable pages.
\f0\b0 \
That distinction will matter enormously when you build your 2nd, 3rd, and 10th company.\
The goal should be:\
