\f1\b\fs48 \cf0 \strokec2 14. What "basic integrations" should mean\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 This is where I'd draw the line.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 Good to include\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs26 \cf0 \
ThemeProvider\
Dark mode\
Light mode\
Responsive behavior\
Form validation\
Client-side validation\
Toast state\
Modal state\
Tabs\
Dropdown state\
Pagination state\
Table sorting\
Table filtering\
Copy-to-clipboard\
Password visibility\
File upload UI\
Command menu\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 Don't include yet\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs26 \cf0 \
Database\
Stripe\
Auth backend\
Redis\
Postgres\
API clients\
Email\
User management\
Cloud storage\
Webhooks\
Server actions\
ORM\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf0 Those belong in the consuming application.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs48 \cf0 \strokec2 15. You can still provide integration adapters later\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

